  "method": {
    "tool": "Lighthouse 13.4.1",
    "preset": "Lighthouse default (mobile emulation, simulated slow-4G throttling)",
    "runsPerPage": 3,
    "aggregation": "median of clean runs; failed runs discarded and re-run, not averaged in",
    "chromeFlags": "--headless=new --disable-gpu",
    "authenticatedMethod": "puppeteer-core seeds sessionStorage authToken/currentUser via evaluateOnNewDocument, then Lighthouse startFlow navigates the same tab with disableStorageReset:true. Each authenticated report was verified to have a finalDisplayedUrl on the intended page, not a redirect to /login."
  },
  "knownIssuesFoundDuringCapture": [
    "PRODUCTION BUG: the Cloudflare Worker origin (https://trailpack---smart-camping-trip-planner.shrey30patel.workers.dev) is NOT in the backend's CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. Preflight OPTIONS /trips from that origin answers 403, so every authenticated feature is broken on that deployment. The Vercel origin is allowed and works. Authenticated baselines were therefore captured on Vercel only.",
    "Unauthenticated Lighthouse runs are flaky in this environment: 6 of the first 24 runs failed NO_FCP and were re-run with spacing between launches."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Worker and Vercel serve byte-identical HTML; any difference between them is CDN/network only.",
    "Authenticated pages were measured against a throwaway account seeded via the public API and deleted immediately afterward. The trip held 36 checklist items, 11 marked packed.",
    "The checklist page fetches weather, provisions and risk data from external services at load, so its numbers include third-party latency that is outside the frontend code."
  ],
